1
00:00:01,207 --> 00:00:09,247
The Princess Sapphire

2
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,160
♪ Atashi no miru yume himitsu nano ♪
The dreams I see are my secret

3
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,089
♪ Dare ni mo iwanai himitsu nano ♪
I won’t tell anyone—it’s my secret

4
00:00:58,541 --> 00:01:02,461
♪ Akai manto hira hira ♪
A red cape fluttering

5
00:01:02,462 --> 00:01:04,981
♪ Uma o tobasu oujo ♪
Galloping on a horse—the princess

6
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:06,901
♪ Sore ga atashi ♪
That’s me!

7
00:01:07,621 --> 00:01:10,901
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

8
00:01:10,905 --> 00:01:13,424
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

9
00:01:14,541 --> 00:01:18,021
♪ Lula-dula-lula-dula ♪
-

10
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:20,741
♪ Lulu laa, lulaa ♪
-

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:25,220
♪ Ribon no kishi wa ♪
The Princess Knight,

12
00:01:25,220 --> 00:01:28,621
♪ Honto wa hontto wa ♪
Truly, truly,

13
00:01:28,622 --> 00:01:31,822
♪ Atashi nano sa ♪
It’s really me!

14
00:01:44,101 --> 00:01:50,141
Thirty-Fifth Episode
The Weapon of Death

15
00:02:30,741 --> 00:02:35,895
- I’m going faster!
- No! I’m going faster!

16
00:02:35,941 --> 00:02:38,933
- No, that's not true!
- Yes, it is!

17
00:02:38,981 --> 00:02:40,733
I'll get there first!

18
00:02:41,261 --> 00:02:43,491
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!

19
00:02:54,261 --> 00:02:57,094
Looks like there's some fun to
be had, old man! Let's go too!

20
00:02:57,141 --> 00:02:58,813
Yes, let’s go!

21
00:02:58,861 --> 00:03:01,011
- What do those two want to do?
- I don't know.

22
00:03:01,781 --> 00:03:04,739
- We're coming too! Are you ready?
- Yes, ready!

23
00:03:05,781 --> 00:03:08,898
Go! Go! Come on!

24
00:03:10,021 --> 00:03:12,489
I'm winning! I'm telling you, I'm winning!

25
00:03:14,421 --> 00:03:16,935
I'm the only one left! I won!

26
00:03:17,061 --> 00:03:19,256
Here's the winner!

27
00:03:19,301 --> 00:03:21,610
- Brake! Brake!
- Pull the brake!

28
00:03:21,661 --> 00:03:24,334
Pull the brake, old man!
Pull the brake!

29
00:03:24,381 --> 00:03:29,250
What? "Pull the brake"?!
But how do I stop?! Help!

30
00:03:32,821 --> 00:03:35,255
This thing won't stop!

31
00:03:39,901 --> 00:03:41,732
Poor old man!

32
00:03:41,781 --> 00:03:44,579
I'll catch that road pirate!

33
00:03:45,021 --> 00:03:47,660
Wait! Wait!

34
00:03:47,701 --> 00:03:51,011
- Hey, old man!
- Poor guy!

35
00:03:51,061 --> 00:03:54,053
Damn it! Who treated the old man like this?

36
00:03:54,821 --> 00:03:57,289
Look here! What is this thing?

37
00:03:58,541 --> 00:04:01,772
It fell from the road pirate's carriage.

38
00:04:08,181 --> 00:04:10,900
Wait, you coward! Wait!

39
00:04:13,541 --> 00:04:15,532
I'll catch you!

40
00:04:23,141 --> 00:04:25,291
Hit and run, eh?

41
00:04:39,101 --> 00:04:42,138
If I had arrived any later,
you would have certainly died, old man.

42
00:04:42,181 --> 00:04:44,012
Thank God...!

43
00:04:44,061 --> 00:04:47,098
I couldn't catch up to
that carriage, I'm sorry.

44
00:04:47,181 --> 00:04:49,775
Don't worry,
I'll catch it, old man!

45
00:04:49,821 --> 00:04:52,460
He dropped this
behind that carriage!

46
00:04:52,501 --> 00:04:55,015
Maybe we can find out who it was
with this!

47
00:04:56,501 --> 00:05:00,858
Let's go, Sapphire! Let's look for him
together! I'll knock him down!

48
00:05:04,381 --> 00:05:06,497
We searched all day,

49
00:05:06,541 --> 00:05:09,419
but we didn't find anyone
who knows about the carriage.

50
00:05:09,461 --> 00:05:12,453
Cheer up, Sapphire!
Today we'll find a way

51
00:05:12,501 --> 00:05:14,651
- Yes, of course.
...for the old man.

52
00:05:23,341 --> 00:05:26,094
- Go away, brat!
- Help!

53
00:05:26,261 --> 00:05:28,297
Look, Choppy is here!

54
00:05:28,341 --> 00:05:32,619
What drug do you want to buy with only
10 Yen? You're a pathetic idiot!

55
00:05:32,661 --> 00:05:35,892
Don't call me an idiot!
You're the idiot!

56
00:05:37,301 --> 00:05:40,930
Heavenly Father, forgive me
for calling him an "idiot"!

57
00:05:41,341 --> 00:05:45,254
- Choppy!
- Opal! Sapphire!

58
00:05:45,301 --> 00:05:47,895
Tell me, Choppy:
what is this story about a drug?

59
00:05:48,021 --> 00:05:51,218
My friends, the rabbit
and the badger, were run over..

60
00:05:51,261 --> 00:05:54,412
...by a carriage.
It was a black carriage, a horrible one!

61
00:05:55,021 --> 00:05:57,581
What did you say?
A black carriage?!

62
00:06:08,021 --> 00:06:10,376
Poor things, I feel sorry for them!

63
00:06:10,421 --> 00:06:13,254
They are looking for whoever hit you. Do you know anything about it?

64
00:06:17,780 --> 00:06:19,817
I understand, thank you.

65
00:06:19,860 --> 00:06:22,136
He said they don't know whose carriage it is,

66
00:06:22,180 --> 00:06:25,730
but that it passes through the Northern forest every day at the same time.

67
00:06:27,420 --> 00:06:29,298
The Northern forest?

68
00:06:36,740 --> 00:06:39,494
- They're right, it passes through here.
- True.

69
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:42,854
Look, these leaves haven't been trampled!

70
00:06:44,020 --> 00:06:46,296
It means it hasn't passed yet.

71
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,299
A noise!

72
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:52,296
It's coming from that direction!

73
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,893
Listen...

74
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:57,218
You're great!

75
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:11,532
Come on!

76
00:07:15,780 --> 00:07:18,011
It's the forest behind the castle!

77
00:07:22,940 --> 00:07:26,820
It's strange... No one is allowed
to use the back gate.

78
00:07:31,420 --> 00:07:33,218
Strange...!

79
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,937
- Open up! Open up!
- What do you want, child?

80
00:07:43,060 --> 00:07:45,814
- Open the gate!
- It's forbidden to open it!

81
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:49,300
But a black carriage just passed by!

82
00:07:49,340 --> 00:07:51,332
No, no one passed.

83
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:55,340
You're a liar! I saw it!
Open! Open the door!

84
00:07:55,500 --> 00:07:57,731
Keep your mouth shut
and go home!

85
00:07:57,780 --> 00:08:00,170
Damn you, open up! Open up!

86
00:08:00,340 --> 00:08:03,219
Fine, then I'll wait here!
There!

87
00:08:03,820 --> 00:08:07,700
Until you've decided
to open that damn gate!

88
00:08:27,820 --> 00:08:30,289
It looks like it fell
right from here.

89
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:34,012
This is definitely the
carriage and that is the culprit.

90
00:08:36,860 --> 00:08:38,499
There's a ladder!

91
00:08:40,820 --> 00:08:43,335
I wonder where
this corridor leads...

92
00:08:54,941 --> 00:08:58,377
- Are you sure no one saw you?
- Yes, don't worry.

93
00:08:59,221 --> 00:09:01,098
It's Geralamon!

94
00:09:04,021 --> 00:09:06,012
Someone is coming!

95
00:09:09,901 --> 00:09:11,857
I wonder who it is..!

96
00:09:16,021 --> 00:09:17,818
It's my father!

97
00:09:17,861 --> 00:09:20,295
Oh, what a pleasure to see
Your Majesty!

98
00:09:22,301 --> 00:09:25,020
What could my father possibly
have to discuss, in private,

99
00:09:25,061 --> 00:09:27,052
with those two scoundrels?

100
00:09:27,301 --> 00:09:29,690
I hope it isn't something bad.

101
00:09:29,901 --> 00:09:31,892
I hope so with all my heart.

102
00:09:36,421 --> 00:09:39,140
So, Your Majesty,
I will deliver it into your hands

103
00:09:39,181 --> 00:09:42,935
...as soon as it is completed.
- Very well, I understand.

104
00:09:48,541 --> 00:09:51,135
- May I go now?
- Of course.

105
00:09:59,021 --> 00:10:03,890
Stop! Tell me what you were
discussing with the King and Geralamon!

106
00:10:04,661 --> 00:10:07,812
That means you are a spy,
if you want to know the agreements...

107
00:10:07,861 --> 00:10:10,739
...that I made for the new
weapons I invented.

108
00:10:10,901 --> 00:10:13,176
- On guard!
- I am not a spy!

109
00:10:13,221 --> 00:10:16,338
I am a friend of the old man
whom your carriage ran over.

110
00:10:17,021 --> 00:10:20,650
So much fuss
over that stupid accident!

111
00:10:20,701 --> 00:10:24,137
I have come to punish you for the wrong
you did to the old man!

112
00:10:26,341 --> 00:10:29,139
You are insolent and a fool!

113
00:10:30,101 --> 00:10:32,092
On guard!

114
00:10:36,021 --> 00:10:38,694
It seems your back is against the wall!

115
00:10:42,821 --> 00:10:44,812
I am here!

116
00:10:57,021 --> 00:10:59,012
Don't run away, you coward!

117
00:10:59,421 --> 00:11:03,733
I'm not running! I want to show you
how my new weapon works!

118
00:11:03,781 --> 00:11:06,056
- Come on!
- Here it is!

119
00:11:11,021 --> 00:11:14,696
- Well? Is that all?
- Damn it!

120
00:11:16,461 --> 00:11:18,691
I have many others
even more powerful!

121
00:11:18,741 --> 00:11:20,732
Let me see how they work!

122
00:11:25,301 --> 00:11:27,019
What... What is it?
- It's a rifle

123
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:30,940
It's a birdlime gun, one of
my most amusing inventions!

124
00:11:31,821 --> 00:11:34,540
It's not fair that you use
such strange weapons!

125
00:11:35,741 --> 00:11:39,177
Have fun, I have things to do.
See you!

126
00:11:40,861 --> 00:11:43,375
Don't run away, you coward!

127
00:11:43,421 --> 00:11:45,298
It's so sticky!

128
00:11:45,341 --> 00:11:48,856
This is a wine barrel!
Maybe the wine will dissolve the birdlime!

129
00:11:54,701 --> 00:11:56,657
Hurray, it worked!

130
00:11:57,501 --> 00:12:00,937
Princess Sapphire,
you shouldn't use that gate!

131
00:12:01,181 --> 00:12:05,299
But this is an emergency! Boy,
which way did the carriage go?

132
00:12:05,741 --> 00:12:08,096
Calm down! Calm down!

133
00:12:09,901 --> 00:12:12,176
What a terrible smell!

134
00:12:12,821 --> 00:12:16,700
- It's a foul-smelling fruit!
- Truly!

135
00:12:17,301 --> 00:12:19,815
It's our lucky break!
When the carriage left,

136
00:12:19,861 --> 00:12:22,739
I threw it at it, so
now we can follow its tracks..

137
00:12:22,781 --> 00:12:25,341
...with our sense of smell!
Forgive me, Opal!

138
00:12:37,741 --> 00:12:39,891
We are right
in the middle of the mountains.

139
00:12:39,941 --> 00:12:42,091
I smell a very strong stench

140
00:12:44,221 --> 00:12:46,257
It must be in here

141
00:12:46,341 --> 00:12:48,901
And now how do we
open the door?

142
00:12:49,341 --> 00:12:51,013
Heave!

143
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:53,177
It's not moving at all!

144
00:12:55,181 --> 00:12:59,254
Maybe we can find an entrance
by climbing the mountain.

145
00:13:12,661 --> 00:13:15,573
Flight test! Open the ceiling!

146
00:13:16,101 --> 00:13:18,012
Yes, sir!

147
00:13:28,621 --> 00:13:31,010
I don't think we can enter through here

148
00:13:45,741 --> 00:13:47,732
Look, it's incredible!

149
00:13:51,501 --> 00:13:54,299
The King of Silverland
and Duke Geralamon..

150
00:13:54,341 --> 00:13:58,334
...have finally promised
to buy this aircraft from me!

151
00:14:09,541 --> 00:14:13,136
I congratulate myself
for this masterpiece!

152
00:14:14,421 --> 00:14:17,060
Now I understand! Dad and
Geralamon were arguing...

153
00:14:17,101 --> 00:14:19,490
...whether or not
to buy this aircraft.

154
00:14:20,581 --> 00:14:23,573
I believe it must be a
truly terrible weapon.

155
00:14:37,301 --> 00:14:41,135
Listen, Sapphire: let's get
revenge on that road pirate!

156
00:14:41,621 --> 00:14:44,772
Yes, let's do it! And let's
destroy these terrible weapons!

157
00:14:44,821 --> 00:14:46,459
- I agree!
- Good!

158
00:14:46,501 --> 00:14:48,617
Everything is ready!

159
00:14:51,221 --> 00:14:53,610
Here we are!

160
00:14:55,141 --> 00:14:57,018
What's happening?

161
00:15:00,141 --> 00:15:04,100
Don't run away! They're
just children! Get them!

162
00:15:11,261 --> 00:15:13,729
Hey, the aircraft!
We could destroy it!

163
00:15:13,781 --> 00:15:16,341
You break the pipe and let out the steam.
- Alright!

164
00:15:21,061 --> 00:15:22,733
There!

165
00:15:26,701 --> 00:15:28,373
What?!

166
00:15:40,261 --> 00:15:43,014
- To hell with you!
- Wait!

167
00:15:43,141 --> 00:15:45,735
If you don't put down
that bomb immediately,

168
00:15:45,781 --> 00:15:48,215
- this child will die!
- Sapphire!

169
00:15:48,261 --> 00:15:52,140
- Child!
- Throw it! Don't worry about me!

170
00:15:52,821 --> 00:15:55,016
Well done! That's it!

171
00:15:55,701 --> 00:15:58,169
Now let the child go!

172
00:15:58,341 --> 00:16:00,013
Jump down!

173
00:16:10,221 --> 00:16:12,496
Get rid of that nuisance!

174
00:16:14,021 --> 00:16:15,898
Don't move!

175
00:16:16,461 --> 00:16:18,577
Beat it, quickly!

176
00:16:22,621 --> 00:16:24,339
Wait!

177
00:16:25,901 --> 00:16:27,573
Damn you!

178
00:16:49,701 --> 00:16:52,852
Excellent! The altitude is fine,
the direction too,

179
00:16:52,901 --> 00:16:56,576
- and the engine is in good condition!
- Set me free, you road pirate!

180
00:16:57,541 --> 00:17:00,294
How does it feel
to be on the aircraft?

181
00:17:00,701 --> 00:17:03,135
You damn monster, untie me!

182
00:17:04,421 --> 00:17:07,299
Scream all you want, I'm going to throw you
out of the aircraft anyway,

183
00:17:07,341 --> 00:17:10,731
so you'll have a nice flight
and be crushed on the ground!

184
00:17:10,781 --> 00:17:14,296
On the ground, no!
Help, Sapphire!

185
00:17:15,421 --> 00:17:19,653
Cry as much as you want,
you annoying brat!

186
00:17:29,741 --> 00:17:32,858
Now it's high enough
to throw you down.

187
00:17:34,741 --> 00:17:38,017
My god, it's so high!
Help, Sapphire!

188
00:17:38,861 --> 00:17:41,819
Now you'll take a nice flight
with no return!

189
00:17:41,861 --> 00:17:45,137
Sapphire! Sapphire!

190
00:17:45,701 --> 00:17:47,293
What?!

191
00:17:50,621 --> 00:17:53,010
- I've finally caught up with you!
- That's right, Sapphire!

192
00:17:53,061 --> 00:17:55,495
- Such tenacity!
- Are you alright?

193
00:17:55,541 --> 00:17:58,009
Yes! I knew you'd come to save me!

194
00:17:59,141 --> 00:18:01,780
And now, prepare to die as well!

195
00:18:36,821 --> 00:18:40,257
Hip, hip, hooray!

196
00:18:53,461 --> 00:18:56,294
- Hey, what is that thing?
- It's a balloon!

197
00:18:56,341 --> 00:18:58,411
No, it's a flying ship!

198
00:18:59,381 --> 00:19:03,499
Here, Your Majesty! The flying
boat has been delivered. Look!

199
00:19:03,541 --> 00:19:05,577
I told you we could trust them.

200
00:19:05,621 --> 00:19:07,851
Isn't it beautiful?

201
00:19:08,021 --> 00:19:10,171
Oh, but it's terrible!

202
00:19:29,941 --> 00:19:33,820
- Princess Sapphire!
- Sapphire, what are you doing here?

203
00:19:33,861 --> 00:19:37,456
I arrested the driver, because
he wanted to kill this child.

204
00:19:41,021 --> 00:19:45,094
How did it occur to you, father,
to order such a terrible weapon

205
00:19:45,141 --> 00:19:47,177
from such a horrible man?!

206
00:19:47,981 --> 00:19:51,257
Don't be foolish, Princess!
That man is a genius!

207
00:19:51,301 --> 00:19:53,610
He has built
some extremely powerful weapons!

208
00:19:53,661 --> 00:19:57,051
No one will be able to defeat us if we
are in possession of those weapons!

209
00:19:57,101 --> 00:19:59,012
- No country!
- Shut up!

210
00:19:59,061 --> 00:20:01,814
He who makes weapons to kill
is far from being a genius!

211
00:20:01,861 --> 00:20:05,536
Your Majesty, do not pay attention
to what a child says!

212
00:20:05,581 --> 00:20:08,015
Please, release that man
and make sure he can...

213
00:20:08,061 --> 00:20:11,337
...continue to build for us
ever more powerful weapons!

214
00:20:11,381 --> 00:20:14,339
Give him money
and, if you don't have enough,

215
00:20:14,381 --> 00:20:16,576
impose a few more taxes.

216
00:20:16,621 --> 00:20:20,660
Damn you! Who are you to impose
taxes on the poor like us...

217
00:20:20,821 --> 00:20:23,016
...to pay a monster
like that?!

218
00:20:23,061 --> 00:20:25,017
But we need
to become strong.

219
00:20:25,061 --> 00:20:27,894
Other countries could attack us
at any moment,

220
00:20:27,941 --> 00:20:30,409
so we need
good weapons.

221
00:20:30,821 --> 00:20:34,575
We don't need the aircraft
to become stronger.

222
00:20:34,621 --> 00:20:37,215
And nobody, then, could
stop that man...

223
00:20:37,261 --> 00:20:39,377
...from building others
for other countries.

224
00:20:40,741 --> 00:20:43,699
Your Majesty, it is not the time
to listen to a little girl!

225
00:20:43,741 --> 00:20:46,619
- Your Majesty!
- Father, listen...

226
00:20:47,301 --> 00:20:49,610
Open up! He's escaped!

227
00:20:52,461 --> 00:20:55,851
That's enough! I've decided that
I will no longer sell you this aircraft!

228
00:20:55,901 --> 00:20:58,256
I'm going to sell it to another country!

229
00:20:58,301 --> 00:21:01,338
What do you want to do? Do
you want to sell it to our enemies?!

230
00:21:01,381 --> 00:21:04,339
That's exactly what I'll do! Goodbye!

231
00:21:04,581 --> 00:21:08,017
Wait! We'll buy it! Wait!

232
00:21:10,781 --> 00:21:12,851
Now get out, if you can!

233
00:21:14,901 --> 00:21:19,133
Damn you, let me go!
Let me go!

234
00:21:19,501 --> 00:21:22,618
No, I won't let you go!

235
00:21:24,461 --> 00:21:27,021
Untie the rope, please!

236
00:21:27,061 --> 00:21:30,292
I beg you! Untie the rope!

237
00:21:30,461 --> 00:21:32,611
I beg you!

238
00:21:33,021 --> 00:21:37,890
No! I won't allow you to sell
the aircraft to some other country!

239
00:21:38,421 --> 00:21:41,891
Damn it!
I'll untie that rope!

240
00:21:57,301 --> 00:22:01,579
Damn it! All this work lost!
The fire!

241
00:22:02,701 --> 00:22:04,896
Put out the fire!

242
00:22:06,501 --> 00:22:10,210
If he reaches the
aircraft, I am lost!

243
00:22:10,261 --> 00:22:12,695
Help me!

244
00:22:32,901 --> 00:22:36,211
Peace to his soul. Amen.

245
00:22:40,341 --> 00:22:42,332
Poor man..!

246
00:22:44,101 --> 00:22:46,899
Old man, the
road pirate is dead.

247
00:22:46,941 --> 00:22:50,411
- Now you can forgive him.
- What a great loss!

248
00:22:50,461 --> 00:22:52,929
- Fools!
- You are mad!

249
00:22:53,741 --> 00:22:56,539
Sapphire, you were right.
Horrible weapons like that...

250
00:22:56,581 --> 00:23:00,051
...do not make us stronger. Other
countries would make even more deadly ones.

251
00:23:00,661 --> 00:23:03,619
Father, we do not need
new, horrible weapons.

252
00:23:03,661 --> 00:23:07,256
To defend the country, my
arm and my heart will be enough.

253
00:23:07,301 --> 00:23:09,019
Well done, Sapphire!

254
00:23:09,061 --> 00:23:11,177
Your words make
me ashamed of myself.

255
00:23:11,221 --> 00:23:14,372
Now I am determined to do
anything so that the country...

256
00:23:14,421 --> 00:23:17,538
...may live more happily. Do you
want to help me, my daughter?

257
00:23:17,581 --> 00:23:20,254
- Of course, father! With pleasure!
- I am happy about that.

258
00:23:20,461 --> 00:23:23,737
- I will always support you, Sapphire!
- Thank you.

259
00:23:24,421 --> 00:23:27,413
It means that we will work
together, all three of us.

260
00:23:27,461 --> 00:23:29,019
All right!

261
00:23:55,900 --> 00:23:59,520
♪ Tarari Ratta Ritta Ratta Rattattaa ♪
-

262
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:02,881
♪ Kyahoo! Kyahoo! Kyahoo! ♪
Yahoo! Yahoo! Yahoo!

263
